We're adding a per-chat cache for MPN searches, using the state we already store in conversation_context. There's no new table and no new column.
How it works
The user uploads MPNs or asks a question. We clean each MPN: trim, uppercase, remove spaces.
We check the chat's saved state for MPNs we've already searched.
Valid ones (less than 24 hours old) are reused, with no web search.
Only new or expired MPNs go to the web search, a few at a time.
New results are added to the state and saved once at the end of the turn, by the existing save.
Only the MPNs in the current question go to the LLM, not the whole cache.
Old turns in the transcript are shortened to one line each, so the saved data doesn't keep growing.
Result: if a user uploads 100 MPNs and later asks about 5 of them, those 5 come from the saved results with zero new searches. A new chat starts empty, so chats never share results.
